{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{x}^{2}+5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+5\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+5(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ee7d8d7f66c3ec4d500febf0f9a0e2ef8fe40b2419ae5dcd01cad8adea78c3"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{13}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/bd73ecb5633b2d3e43637ab5be7dacb6cd69d96957fbc199b0d59bbe6dbbcbec.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ee7d8d7f66c3ec4d500febf0f9a0e2ef8fe40b2419ae5dcd01cad8adea78c3"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-49348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/eb35df379a8d7a20b9003218ee65e1cdcc3849af919805795dab380441d32795.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What are the values of $a$ and $b?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{b}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To get $a$ and $b$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ee7d8d7f66c3ec4d500febf0f9a0e2ef8fe40b2419ae5dcd01cad8adea78c3"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$a=-1$, $b=1$"] ["text" "$a=-3$, $b=3$"] ["text" "$a=-\\sqrt{3}$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$"] ["text" "$a=0$, $b=2$"] ["text" "$a=0$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-54472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$a=-\\sqrt{3}$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/d787ab7b213815ceb2cee11cf3f4a629c0f24b8328b33ae773be1e63f9f9a517.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{-2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ee7d8d7f66c3ec4d500febf0f9a0e2ef8fe40b2419ae5dcd01cad8adea78c3"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-73329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-345320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/927b979152097aef3939fa78738dbd2deb9d297cadf2d9894c19f31ca76aee1b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-345320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+x){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0) \\\\  & =(1+\\pi )-(-1) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-345320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60ee7d8d7f66c3ec4d500febf0f9a0e2ef8fe40b2419ae5dcd01cad8adea78c3"} {"question" "q-345320" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"} {"question" "q-345320" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi+2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c0abf569fe865f1373506a4ca6193b39f3a58c784435bf03f1e6e3bdf8fa891"}] "usage" {"q-49348" [] "q-11005" []} "basis" 1310 "retractions" [[17592186096867 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/q-11005.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y =-3x^{2} + 5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x = 1$, shown above."] [17592186097198 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/q-49348.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y = \\cos x$ and the $x$-axis between $x = \\frac{π}{2}$ and $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093610 17592186093611 17592186093612 17592186